# Current events in town, by region, part two: Westmarch, Lakeside, Fenhollow, Amberford, Hollowmere, the three
# fortresses and the ghost town.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Westmarch

scene et_wm_theft_sheep
when topic=crime kind=theft region=westmarch
a : Rustlers on the downs again. {victim} lost six head. | {victim}'s flock came back short by a dozen. | Somebody's driving stolen sheep east by night.
b[herder] : I'll sleep out with mine and my crook. Let them try.
b[guard] : We'll ride the barrow road at dusk. They use it, the cowards.
b : Six! That's a winter's living. | A dozen! | East, toward the drovers' road.
a : A whole winter. | Gone in a night. | Easy to sell there.

scene et_wm_arrest_frontier
when topic=crime kind=arrest region=westmarch
a : They've locked {subject} in the old watch house. | {subject}'s taken. Westmarch looks after its own, and deals with its own. | The Mercantile pressed charges on {subject}, I hear.
b : That watch house leaks. Good. | We do. | The Mercantile presses everyone.
a : Very good. | Always have. | Half the downs owes it.

scene et_wm_death_barrows
when topic=life kind=death region=westmarch
a : They'll lay {subject} by the old barrows. With the ancestors. | Lights on the barrows the night {subject} died. I saw them. | {subject}'s gone. The downs feel emptier.
b[old] : The barrows take their own. Always have, long before the chapel.
b[priest] : The Bright One keeps them, not the barrows. But I'll say the words there.
b : With the old ones. Right. | You saw nothing but marsh gas. | They do.
a : Right and proper. | I know what I saw. | Wide and empty.

scene et_wm_newcomer_frontier
when topic=newcomer region=westmarch
a : {subject} rode in from the east. Says they want land. | {subject}'s a city wolf. You can tell by the boots. | {subject} asked about the barrows. First thing.
b[herder] : Land's free out here. Keeping it is the hard part.
b : Plenty of it. Not much grows. | They'll have mud on them by sundown. | Tell them to stay off them.
a : Grass, mostly. | And blisters. | I did.

scene et_wm_festival_drovers
when topic=festival region=westmarch
a : The drovers time their run to be here for {festival}. | Bonfires on every hill of the downs for {festival}. | The Last Lantern stays open all night for {festival}.
b[innkeeper] : I'll sleep after {festival}. Some time next week.
b : Cattle and ale. Westmarch feasting. | You can see them for leagues. | It always does.
a : The best kind. | Like stars on the ground. | All night.

scene et_wm_gossip
when topic=gossip region=westmarch
a : Out on the downs they're saying {subject} {claim}. | The drovers swear {subject} {claim}. | At the Mercantile counter: {subject} {claim}.
b : Not much else to talk about out there. | Drovers swear about everything. | The counter's where truth goes to die.
a : Sheep and gossip. | Mostly cattle. | And ledgers.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Lakeside

scene et_ls_theft_boat
when topic=crime kind=theft region=lakeside
a : Somebody's been taking boats at night again. {victim}'s this time. | {victim} lost the whole catch off the racks. | They took {victim}'s nets right off the jetty.
b[fisher] : Mist hides a thief better than any cloak.
b[soldier] : Could be garrison lads. Bored, drunk, a long row home.
b : The mist covers everything. | The whole catch? | Jetty's never watched.
a : Everything. | Every fish. | It is now.

scene et_ls_death_mere
when topic=life kind=death region=lakeside
a : The mere took {subject}. Went out in the mist. Never came back. | They found {subject}'s skiff drifting by the reeds. | {subject}'s gone. The Mirrormere's still as glass, like nothing happened.
b[fisher] : The mere's calm until it isn't. Every fisher knows it.
b : The mist. Always the mist. | Empty, I suppose. | It doesn't care. It's water.
a : Always. | Empty. | It doesn't.

scene et_ls_newcomer_garrison
when topic=newcomer region=lakeside
a : {subject} came across from the isle. Done their service, staying. | {subject} wants to learn boatbuilding. | {subject} rowed in with the supply boat and never rowed back.
b[soldier] : The isle does that. You serve, then you can't face the open roads.
b : Plenty like that. | A good trade. | Deserter?
a : Plenty. | It is. | Or just tired.

scene et_ls_festival_lanterns
when topic=festival region=lakeside
a : Lanterns floating on the mere for {festival}. One for every soul lost. | The garrison rows over for {festival}. Every year. | Boat races across the mere for {festival}!
b[child] : Can I light a lantern? Can I push it out?
b : It's beautiful. And sad. | They drink us dry. | My cousin's rowing!
a : Both. | Always. | Good luck to them.

scene et_ls_gossip
when topic=gossip region=lakeside
a : The garrison lads swear {subject} {claim}. | On the jetty this morning: {subject} {claim}. | Mist and whispers. {subject} {claim}.
b : The garrison's bored. They'll say anything. | The jetty hears everything. | Fits the weather.
a : Anything. | Everything. | It does.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Fenhollow

scene et_fh_theft_cures
when topic=crime kind=theft region=fenhollow
a : Somebody stole {victim}'s dried bogmyrtle. A season's cures. | Peat stolen off the stacks. Who steals peat? | {victim} was robbed on the causeway at dusk.
b[healer] : They'll poison themselves with it if they don't know the dose.
b : A season's work. | Somebody cold. | The causeway's lonely at dusk.
a : All gone. | Cold and shameless. | Very lonely.

scene et_fh_death_marsh
when topic=life kind=death region=fenhollow
a : {subject} followed the marsh lights. They found them in the bog. | Fever took {subject}. The fen fever. | They're burying {subject} on the dry rise behind the chapel.
b[old] : Never follow the lights. My grandmother said it, and her grandmother.
b : Never follow the lights. | That fever's cruel. | Only dry ground left.
a : Never. | So cruel. | And not much of it.

scene et_fh_newcomer_cure
when topic=newcomer region=fenhollow
a : {subject} came for the marsh cures and decided to stay. | {subject} wants to learn the herbs. Brave, in this damp. | {subject} came in by the causeway, soaked to the knees.
b[healer] : I'll teach them. The fen gives as much as it takes.
b : The cures work, some of them. | They'll grow webbed paws. | Everyone does, first time.
a : Some. | Ha! | Every time.

scene et_fh_festival
when topic=festival region=fenhollow
a : They burn peat bonfires for {festival}. Smoke for a week. | Reed crowns for {festival}! I'm weaving mine. | The causeway's lined with torches for {festival}.
b[child] : My crown's bigger than yours!
b : Smells like home. | Show me when it's done. | Pretty, on the water.
a : Smoky home. | Soon. | Reflections everywhere.

scene et_fh_gossip
when topic=gossip region=fenhollow
a : Bogmyrtle says {subject} {claim}. She's never wrong. | At the peat cutting: {subject} {claim}. | Damp talk, but they say {subject} {claim}.
b : Bogmyrtle's wrong half the time. | Peat cutters gossip like crows. | Everything's damp here.
a : Never to her face. | Worse. | Even the talk.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Amberford

scene et_af_theft_grain
when topic=crime kind=theft region=amberford
a : Somebody broke into the granary. {victim}'s grain. | Grain sacks gone from {victim}'s barn. In a drought! | They took the toll box from the ford.
b[farmer] : A thief in a dry year's worse than a thief in a wet one.
b[official] : The toll box! That's the watch's wages.
b : The granary! In this drought? | Shameless. | The whole box?
a : Shameless. | Utterly. | Every penny.

scene et_af_death
when topic=life kind=death region=amberford
a : {subject} died in the fields. Heat took them. | They found {subject} in the ford. The water's so low, how? | {subject}'s gone. They'll be buried under the old oak.
b[farmer] : The sun's no friend this year.
b : This heat'll kill us all. | Low water still drowns. | The oak's seen a lot of us off.
a : It might. | Always does. | It has.

scene et_af_newcomer
when topic=newcomer region=amberford
a : {subject} came to help with the harvest. Says they'll stay. | {subject} asked to rent a field. In a drought. | New wolf at the mill. {subject}.
b[farmer] : Strong back? Then welcome.
b : Good. We need paws. | Brave or foolish. | The miller needed help.
a : We do. | Foolish. | Good.

scene et_af_festival_harvest
when topic=festival region=amberford
a : The last sheaf goes on the hall door for {festival}. | Barn dance for {festival}! | The miller's grinding sweet flour for the {festival} loaves.
b[farmer] : Even in a dry year, we feast. That's the point.
b : Good luck for the year. | I'll bring my fiddle. | Golden loaves.
a : It needs it. | Please do. | Amber loaves.

scene et_af_gossip
when topic=gossip region=amberford
a : At the mill they're saying {subject} {claim}. | Over the hedgerow: {subject} {claim}. | The toll-keeper says {subject} {claim}.
b : The mill's worse than a tavern. | Hedges have ears. | Toll-keepers see everyone.
a : Dustier, too. | Long ones. | And tell everyone.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Hollowmere

scene et_hm_theft
when topic=crime kind=theft region=hollowmere_village
a : A thief? In Hollowmere? {victim}, of all wolves. | Nobody steals in Hollowmere. And yet {victim}'s robbed. | Must be someone passing through. Nobody here would rob {victim}.
b[old] : Six generations, no lock on a single door. Now this.
b : Strange days. | And yet. | Must be.
a : Strange. | It's wrong. | Must be.

scene et_hm_life
when topic=life region=hollowmere_village
a : The whole valley knows about {subject} by now. | {subject}! Did you hear? Of course you did. | News travels slow here, except about {subject}.
b : There are only forty of us. | Course I did. | That's the only news.
a : Forty, give or take. | Course you did. | Only news all {season}.

scene et_hm_newcomer
when topic=newcomer region=hollowmere_village
a : {subject} came up the valley road. Nobody comes to Hollowmere by accident. | A newcomer! {subject}! First in years. | {subject} asked if the carter comes often.
b[old] : Last newcomer was my wife. Forty years back.
b : Then why did they come? | Years! | Ha. Did you tell them the truth?
a : We'll find out. | Years and years. | I told them to be patient.

scene et_hm_festival
when topic=festival region=hollowmere_village
a : Just us and a fiddle for {festival}. Best kind of feast. | The whole valley eats together for {festival}. | Bonfire by the brook for {festival}.
b : The very best. | Every family brings a dish. | The brook sings for it.
a : Small and warm. | And everybody eats. | It does.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The fortresses

scene et_ft_newcomer_recruit
when topic=newcomer region=fortresses
a : New recruit came in with the supply cart. {subject}. Green as grass. | {subject}'s been posted here. Looks like they've been sentenced. | Fresh blood. {subject}. Commander's pleased.
b[soldier] : I was green once. Grass grows up into hay. Then you're old.
b : They'll ripen. | Feels like it, at first. | He's pleased with anything that walks.
a : If the cold doesn't take them. | It is, a bit. | And holds a spear.
b?[old] : Give them the bunk by the stove. First winter's the worst.

scene et_ft_newcomer_questions
when topic=newcomer region=fortresses
a : {subject} keeps asking what we're guarding. | {subject} asked when they get leave. | {subject} wanted to know where the tavern is.
b[soldier] : Tell them the same thing they told us. Nothing.
b : Tell them nothing. | Laugh in their face. | There isn't one. Break it gently.
a : I will. | I did. | Poor thing.

scene et_ft_newcomer_veteran
when topic=newcomer region=fortresses
a : {subject} transferred in. Served on the southern border, they say. | {subject}'s a veteran. Scars on scars. | {subject} doesn't talk. Just stands the wall and watches.
b : Good. We need some sense here. | Scars mean they lived. | Best kind of soldier.
a : We do. | They do. | It is.

scene et_ft_newcomer_cook
when topic=newcomer region=fortresses
a : New cook arrived. {subject}. Pray for decent stew. | {subject}'s replacing the old quartermaster. | {subject} came up with the letters. Staying.
b : Anything's better than the last cook. | The old one was a thief anyway. | Brought my letter?
a : Don't say that. It tempts fate. | Everybody knew. | Same as always.

scene et_nf_newcomer_cold
when topic=newcomer region=northern_fortress
a : {subject} arrived in a lowland cloak. They'll freeze by morning. | {subject} asked if it's always this cold. | {subject} saw the moor from the wall and went white.
b[soldier] : Give them a real fur. And the ice-trick for their boots.
b : Lend them a blanket. | Ha. Wait till winter. | Everyone does.
a : I've spare. | It's summer. | First time.

scene et_df_newcomer_deep
when topic=newcomer region=dark_fortress
a : {subject} heard the deep on their first night. Didn't sleep. | {subject} asked about the covered map. Already. | {subject} wants to go below. Don't let them.
b[soldier] : Nobody goes below without the commander. Nobody.
b : None of us did, first night. | Already. Curious one. | I won't.
a : Nor since. | Dangerous trait. | Good.

scene et_if_newcomer_isle
when topic=newcomer region=isle_fortress
a : {subject} got seasick on a lake. A lake! | {subject} rowed over this morning. Already wants to row back. | {subject} asked if the isle's really sinking.
b[soldier] : They all ask that. Tell them we bail it out at night.
b : On the Mirrormere? It was flat calm! | They all do. | Tell them yes.
a : Flat as a plate. | All of us. | I did.

scene et_ft_death
when topic=life kind=death region=fortresses
a : We'll bury {subject} outside the walls, with the others. | Commander's writing to {subject}'s family. | The whole garrison stood for {subject}.
b[soldier] : The wall takes one or two a year. Cold, falls, fever.
b : With the old garrison. | Hard letter to write. | Right and proper.
a : They'll have company. | The hardest. | It is.

scene et_ft_festival
when topic=festival region=fortresses
a : Extra rations for {festival}. Real meat. | Commander gives us a cask for {festival}. One cask, for all of us. | A fiddle on the wall for {festival}. Almost like home.
b[soldier] : One cask, sixty soldiers. Wonderful.
b : Real meat! I'll believe it when I see it. | Share it out careful. | Almost.
a : I saw it. | Careful. | Almost.

scene et_ft_crime
when topic=crime kind=theft|assault region=fortresses
a : Somebody's been at the rations store. {subject}, they say. | There was a fight in the barracks. | Commander's furious. Theft, in a fortress.
b[soldier] : In a garrison? Where would you even hide it?
b : They'll hang them, or worse. | Cabin fever. Always is. | He would be.
a : Worse, probably. | Always. | Furious.

scene et_ft_gossip
when topic=gossip region=fortresses
a : On the wall last night they said {subject} {claim}. | The supply carter says {subject} {claim}. | Barracks talk. {subject} {claim}.
b : Bored soldiers. | Carters gossip like old women. | Barracks talk is barracks talk.
a : Very bored. | Worse. | It passes the night.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The ghost town

scene et_gt_newcomer_squatter
when topic=newcomer region=ghost_town
a : Someone else has moved into the east houses. {subject}. | {subject} turned up in the night. Said they've nowhere else. | Another one, {subject}. This place fills up with nobodies.
b[beggar] : Nobody comes here unless they've nowhere. We're all nowhere folk.
b : More mouths for nothing. | None of us have. | We're all nobodies.
a : Nothing's what we've got. | No. | At least we're together.

scene et_gt_newcomer_wary
when topic=newcomer region=ghost_town
a : I don't like {subject}. They ask too much about why the town emptied. | {subject} reads the names on the chapel door. Out loud. | {subject} sleeps in the old inn. Alone. Brave.
b : Nobody knows why. | Don't do that. It's bad luck. | Or foolish.
a : That's what scares me. | Tell them. | Same thing, here.

scene et_gt_newcomer_share
when topic=newcomer region=ghost_town
a : {subject} brought a sack of turnips. I like them already. | {subject} can fix a roof. That's worth something here. | {subject} lit a fire in the old square. First in a hundred years, maybe.
b : Turnips are friendship. | Worth a lot. | Felt like the place breathed.
a : Turnips are everything. | It is. | It did.

scene et_gt_newcomer_lost
when topic=newcomer region=ghost_town
a : {subject} thought this was a living town. Came for work. | {subject} wandered in off the road. Lost. | {subject} keeps calling into empty houses, like someone will answer.
b : Disappointed, I'd think. | Lost and stayed. Like us. | Someone might.
a : Very. | Like us. | Don't say that.

scene et_gt_crime
when topic=crime kind=theft|assault region=ghost_town
a : Somebody's taking from the shared pot. | Someone took my good blanket. There are four of us! | Things go missing. Wolves, or the town.
b : One of us, then. | Four suspects. | Don't start that.
a : One of us. | Three, not counting me. | It's the town.

scene et_gt_festival
when topic=festival region=ghost_town
a : We'll keep {festival} here. Somebody should, in this place. | A fire and a song for {festival}. Even here. | They must have kept {festival} here once.
b : For the ones who left. | Even here. | Tables still set, like they meant to.
a : For them. | Even here. | Strange to think.
